<item>
            <title>[LU-20877] mdt: remote same-directory rename does not lock the target name</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20877</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;A rename within one directory locks the target name&apos;s PDO bucket only&lt;br/&gt;
when the directory is local to the serving MDT (mdt_lock_two_dirs(),&lt;br/&gt;
the !mdt_object_remote() check).  A same-directory rename is served on&lt;br/&gt;
the MDT of the file at the target name when one exists, so when that&lt;br/&gt;
file lives on another MDT than the directory, the rename holds the&lt;br/&gt;
directory&apos;s CW lock and the source name&apos;s bucket only.  The target&lt;br/&gt;
name can then change between the rename&apos;s lookup of it and its child&lt;br/&gt;
locks, and nothing looks it up again: mdd_rename() deletes the target&lt;br/&gt;
entry by name.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15526&quot; title=&quot;PDO lock for object on remote MDT&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15526&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15526&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (7270e16fcb, 2.16.0) a PW lock on a remote parent is a&lt;br/&gt;
per-name PDO lock; before it, it was a whole-directory lock that&lt;br/&gt;
covered the target name.  From then on an unlink and re-create of the&lt;br/&gt;
target name can change it in the window.  Since &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17427&quot; title=&quot;reduce hold time for BFL rename lock&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-17427&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17427&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (8dbf049479,&lt;br/&gt;
2.17.0) the BFL is taken after the child locks, so another rename&lt;br/&gt;
onto the same name can too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Effect, two clients renaming different files onto one name:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;alternate&quot; type=&quot;square&quot;&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If the file at the target name has no other link, the second rename&lt;br/&gt;
  fails with ENOENT and changes nothing.  POSIX requires it to succeed,&lt;br/&gt;
  so an application replacing a file atomically (write temp, rename&lt;br/&gt;
  over) sees an unexpected error.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;If that file has another hard link, the second rename deletes the&lt;br/&gt;
  entry that now names the first rename&apos;s file and inserts its own.&lt;br/&gt;
  The first rename&apos;s file is left with nlink 1 and no name (an orphan,&lt;br/&gt;
  visible to LFSCK only), and the file the second rename looked up is&lt;br/&gt;
  destroyed while its other hard link still names it.  Both renames&lt;br/&gt;
  return 0.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Reproduced on master with a fail point holding the second rename after&lt;br/&gt;
its target lookup (directory on MDT0, files on MDT1, A/dst hard linked&lt;br/&gt;
as A/keep; mv A/a A/dst and mv A/b A/dst from two mounts): A/dst names&lt;br/&gt;
the second file, A/keep no longer resolves, and the first file is an&lt;br/&gt;
orphan.  The unlink/re-create route follows from the source and is not&lt;br/&gt;
reproduced.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Fix: lock the target name&apos;s bucket for a remote directory too, in hash&lt;br/&gt;
order as &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15285&quot; title=&quot;same dir rename deadlock&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-15285&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-15285&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; does for a local one.  Patch, with regression test&lt;br/&gt;
sanityn 81j: &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69434&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69434&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The parallel cross-MDT file rename change (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20831&quot; title=&quot;mdt: parallel cross-MDT rename of regular files&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20831&quot;&gt;LU-20831&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69203&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/69203&lt;/a&gt;) widens the&lt;br/&gt;
window further by removing the BFL from these renames, and is stacked&lt;br/&gt;
on top of the fix.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
